  "_doc": "184 edits over 92 players: scoring[2026].games +1 and a re-averaged scoring[2026].avg, and NOTHING else. The career `games` field is deliberately untouched \u2014 round_apply._merge_into_store does not touch it either, and an edit that also moved it would be a second writer inventing a rule the ingestor never had. Averages are round((avg*games + score)/(games+1), 2) through the ingestor's OWN `_mean` at the ingestor's OWN ROUND_DECIMALS=2, called rather than restated.",
  "_doc_expected_movers": "THESE COME FROM A REAL BUILD, AND THAT IS SAID RATHER THAN HIDDEN. The first flight of this act declared 234 movers' worth of predictions made by pricing the edit IN MEMORY on a loaded engine, and the builder disagreed: 86 predicted, 234 actual. The in-memory path cannot reproduce the LOAD-TIME CALIBRATION REFIT \u2014 population statistics move when 92 players' averages move, and every valued row shifts a little as a result. That flight built the board and measured the movers before aborting on the declaration, and the tree was restored byte-exact, so this list is what the real builder produced from these exact 184 edits on this exact store. The re-flight is therefore a DETERMINISM assertion, not a prediction: identical inputs must give an identical board, and any drift at all is an abort naming the player."
 },
